  "step_3": "The decision reason requires evaluating outcomes relative to a reference point (here, -500 Euros) and comparing mean differences. The individual does not mention or appear to calculate such differences. While they do reference the sure loss in A and the mixed prospects in B, their focus is on the emotional unattractiveness of a certain loss and a tendency toward risk-seeking in the domain of losses—consistent with prospect theory—but not on computing deviations from the sure outcome as a reference. The justification is more about risk preference under loss than a structured comparison of outcome differences from a reference. There is no evidence of computing or weighing the +500 and -500 deviations around -500. Thus, while the individual considers some of the same elements (sure loss, risky alternative), they do not apply the specific rule of the decision reason. The reasoning is thematically related but structurally distinct.",
